Max change log (1999)
=====================

VERSION HISTORY       
---------------

12/20/99 Max 3.2.7
	made Max 20% more space efficient (by mallocing tiles a block at a time)
	better handling of new colormap:  reduces colormap 'technicolor' problem,
		and reduces restarts of Max.  Allows multiple Maxs to coexist
		peacefully.

12/16/99 Max 3.2.6
	fixed mc2.0
	fixed redisplay stipple bug.
	fixed drc bug (involving null area checks)
	fixed obscure manhattan mitering problem.  
		(now depends on general mitering which is not yet implemented).
	added partial GDS file read capability (can specify which cells to read)
	using new mmi shared config info (first common src multi-platform compile
	 	of Max at MMI)
	improved and cleaned up message handling (more work pending)
	commented out "TODO mitre ... message"

12/5/99 Max 3.2.5
	fixed drc bug.
	
11/16/99 Max 3.2.4
	fixed gcell undo bug.
	fixed :erase usage message
	completed GCELL_WRITE_FLATTEN_GCELLS implementation.

11/8/99 Max 3.2.3
	fixed def name in dup instance name error message
	fixed ruler text problem
	fixed gcell/flyline redisplay problem
	fixed 'hang' on gds output with no layer ops.
	optimized gds output with no layer ops 
	  (not yet exploited by maketech).
	fixed drc 'horizon' bug for area rules.

10/22/99 Max 3.2.2
	fixed Solaris 2.7 xserver crash.	
	fixed frame drift problem (when scrolling etc)
	enabled backing store for layout widgets 
	  (instant redisplay of temporarily obscured areas)
	fixed stipple origin (solves redisplay glitches)
	added clipping of subcell text 
	  (fixes problem where text that sticks out leaves turds)
	no longer read .color_map and .display_styles files
	  (obsoleted by palette code) 

10/8/99 Max 3.2.1
	fixed polygon clipping (fixes polygon inversion problem) 
	fixed db_instance/gcells coredump
	fixed max zoom out coredump
	now announcing full path of tech file being loaded

9/30/99 Max 3.2

9/14/99 Max3.1.5
	added "port" statements to cifinput and cifoutput sections
	of tech file.  (allows label kinds to be preserved)

9/10/99 Max3.1.4
	fixed redisplay coredump problem
	fixed coarse redisplay of drc errors
	fixed overflow problem with drc area check
	maxtcl changes
	 
9/8/99  Max3.1.3
	mc changes
	maxtcl changes
	extractor fixed to output centimicrons

8/25/99 Max3.1.2
	maxtcl changes

8/24/99 Max3.1.1
	MHA's pre-vacation, Max3 BETA RELEASE?

6/11/99 Max2.37 (DAC VERSION)
	Final DAC Version!

	Fixed :identify undo	
	(completes fix of gcell edit undo bug).
 
6/10/99 Max2.36 (DAC VERSION)
	partial fix to gcell edit undo coredump.

6/8/99 Max2.35 (DAC VERSION)
	fixed flyline redisplay

6/7/99 Max2.34 (DAC VERSION)

	added LAY_STIPPLE_SELECTION 
	(causes selection to be stippled, currently styles file dependent)

	fixed undo from submodes problem.

	fixed selection operations when multiple polygons selected

	fixed undo problem with gcells

	added support for polygons in gcells

	fixed one of problem in builtin flag (db_types command).	

5/12/99 Max 2.33
	 implemented db_label
        (support for labels in gcells)

        fixed db_paint to handle subedits properly

        interpolated latest maxtcl changes.

5/4/99 Max 2.32
	fixed DBSearchPaintNew()
	IMPORTANT:  fixes Hierarchical DRC problem, among others.

	fixed core dump on "db_search paint -area"

	fixed db_gcell_notify to handle bboxes properly.

	implemnented db_instance and db_notify 
	(to support fast DEF reading)

	modified redisplay to give cell orientation.
	
	modified redisplay to not slide ports around.

	changed Max core dump log from tools distribution to mmi_local/max/CRASH_LOG 
	(which at least has a chance of being writable).

	modified panic save code to not save out internal gcells.

	added cell_name option to db_cells 
	(speeds up and simplifies cell info queries)  

	added db_bbox command.

	added -tag option to layout annotations.
	(requested for ruler management etc.)

	added -highlights option to lay_changed
	(supports save/restore of selection).

	fixed sel_polygons so undo works properly.
	
	added warnings in documentation about -no_notify options.

	removed obsolete commands:
	:addpath
	:box
	:layers
	:path
	:snap
	:sleep
	:version
	:what
	:writeall

4/23/99 Max 2.31
	added db_paint to allow safe modification of the database
	by gcell generator code.

	fixed bug in :select that could caused Max to hang.
 
	fixed "db_search paint" to work properly during subedits.

	fixed "db_largest_box" to avoid coredumps when started 
	with "space" or when specified layer not present.		

4/20/99 Max 2.30
	annotation capability for layout widgets (text, lines, dots).

	gds_info provides summary info on gds file (for auto gening tech
	file)

	A number of commands to allow complete interactive (tcl level)
	control of the appearance of layers:
		lay_cmap
		lay_layer_styles
		lay_style
		lay_style_groups 
		lay_stipple	
	
	proper handling of "-help" command-line option.

	implemented on-line documentation of global variables 
	(ala text commands)

	replaced coredump when X-server not doing 8-bit colormapped
	graphics with informative message and some debugging info.

	added MN_TYPICAL_WIRE_WIDTH to allow feature size to be
	specified in absence of m1 with rule.  And fixed redisplay
	code to adjust dynamically to any change in this variable.

	fixed coredump when selecting all angle nets.

	fixed bug that caused all angle net selection to jump nets.

	implemented read/write of classed groups.

	implemented general propertys (name/value pairs) for max cells.

	added support for gcells (generated parameterized cells).
	
3/23/99 Max 2.29
	completed (low level) group implementation for polygons and wirepaths.

	completed selection implementation for polygons and wirepaths.

	completed implementation of operations on selection for polygons 
	and wirepaths (e.g. delete, move, copy rotate, array).

	implemented connectivity tracing for polygons and wirepaths.
	
	implemented undo for polygons and wirepaths.

	implemented polygon clipping for redisplay (removes some
	redisplay artifacts).

	fixed bug in cell deletion code that was causing core dumps.

	changed db_cell_delete and documentation so that it's safe
	for users to use.

	added "-version" command line option:  prints out version of
	Max (without license check) and exits. 

	recoded ancestor check routine to take advantage of max2
	database enhancements - may significantly improve database performance?

	minor updates to on-line (text commands) documentation.

	ALL ANGLE TO DO:
		proper handling of endcaps and mitering for wirepaths
		improved selection redisplay 
		user interface for creation/editing
		mask operations (e.g. AND, GROW, SHRINK)
		netlisting/extraction
		drc
	
2/9/99  Max 2.28
	Fixed GDS message processing to avoid zillions of repeated
	messages when something is wrong.

	Reclassified GDS errors to warnings whenever the file was
	partially read, so what was read in gets loaded into the
	Max layout window. 

	Implemented selection for (all-angle) polygons.  

	Implemented selection operations for polygons
	(e.g. delete, move, copy, rotate, array)

	To play with polygons, start Max in developer mode
	(max -develop 1) and see "Developer" menu.

	Note all angle stuff still incomplete:  
	  User interface for creating polygons is very primitive.
	  Selection not implemented for wire paths.
	  No undo for polygon operations.
	
1/13/99 Max 2.27
	Fixed "sel_what labels" bug introduced in Max2.26 that caused
	sram compiler to fail.

	Fixed problem causing remote Xservers to be dropped.
	(currently fixed during gdsRead, will be extended to other operations)

	Implemented redisplay of polygons when zoomed out.

	Created simple types (layers that do not interact
	with others during gds read/write or paint operations).
	Using simple types to optimize painting and gds read operations.

	Incorporated Pat's maxtcl mods (includes nav window fix, and
	support for tk8).

	Incorporated Pats change that allows maxtcl code to be read
	from ~/mmi_private/max/maxtcl when in Max developer mode.
	Lee NOTE:  you can now hack/test maxtcl code by copying maxtcl/ 
	from ~/mha/max2/ to ~tavrow/mmi_private/max/

	Added mn_path_find tcl command to support path based lookups 
	for Lef/Def etc. 
	Lee NOTE: use "mn_path_find $MN_PATH_CELL foo.lef"  
 
	upgraded to Mega Cell compiler version 1.1

	Added mn_load_mc and hacked Mega Cell compiler to not check
	out license until first invocation.
	NOTE: need to add "mc_init" to .maxrc at installations using
	Mega Cell compiler.

	Now checking license versions for max, maxDev, and mc.

	Changed copyright notice (its 1999 :-)


